immediately jump in and start using it. Because you spend a few weeks learning something, but then you're going to use this tool for the rest of your life. And so, you know, paying the upfront learning cost was fine. And nowadays, we're much more impatient, we're much more expecting sort of immediate gratification at the starting point, even though in fact, experience has taught us that it really does take weeks or years even for people to really acquire mastery of a lot of these tools. We look at something like Adobe Photoshop or any of these 3D modeling and editing programs, and they really do take months and months and years and years to become truly skilled at them. Yeah, that makes sense.
但不管怎样，我想，其实我可以更改航班计划，飞往旧金山。我可以顺便跟着汤姆去参观卢卡斯影业。然后我们可以上去看望我的家人，接着开车去阿纳海姆，而这正是我们最后做的事情。所以我真的这么做了，就像个跟屁虫一样跟着去了。我得以参观了卢卡斯影业的办公室，并在参观时结识了那里的一些人。我的意思是，我们基本上就是（你知道的）技术游客。但那里真的很棒。我的意思是，他们有VAX计算机。

