of it was done with wire app prototyping boards. And there was a utility called wire app that ran on the University of Michigan time sharing system, where you would specify you basically you transcribe your circuit schematic into a macro language that said you're using the following gates and chips and other things. There were macros that encoded the geometry of the chips, which pins were connected to which inputs and which outputs. And then you would specify the logical connectivity of this device in this textual macro language.
你知道的，有一次我问为什么，甚至有些根本没人坐的办公桌上也摆着这么大的显示器。我问他们，为什么后勤部门要在所有的办公桌上都放上巨大的显示器？有人告诉我的一件事非常有趣，他们说，因为当候选人来这里面试时，看到所有这些巨大且昂贵的显示器，他们会觉得，哦，这些人拥有很酷的设备，这一定是一个非常酷的工作地点。我以前完全没有从这个角度想过，直到有人说出来，这感觉有点像看到米老鼠摘下了面具一样。

